\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 A little after ten in the morning, \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
three white Continentals decorated for Christmas turned off the Great Western Goat Track and were waved down by a UDF checkpoint just north of the railway bridge. \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 \'93Purpose of visit?\'94 challenged a lieutenant with an Austeyr rifle slung over her shoulder.\
\'93Christmas,\'94 said the Tulsa McLean driver, who had unfortunately or serendipitously worn his uniform for the occasion.\
\'93And who will you be staying with?\'94\
\'93The Holy Momma.\'94\
\'93The Holy\'97\'94\
\'93\'97Momma.\'94\
\'93And you are?\'94\
\'93Three wise Elvi.\'94\
The lieutenant looked past the driver. \'93There are six of you.\'94\
\'93We\'92re a double act,\'94 the Tulsa said.\
The car was full, and everyone was carrying a sleeping bag or an Esky. The passenger side occupant had a guitar case wedged between his legs. One Elvis in the back seat had his elbow on  a Cabbage Patch baby Jesus. \
\'93Pop the trunk, please driver.\'94\
The Tulsa complied, and two more fresh UDF graduates went round back of the car.\
In the boot were tents and camping gear, and a couple of guitar amplifiers.\
The UDF detail searched the other two cars and found more of the same. By the time they had waved the Lincolns through, a couple of Cadillacs had pulled up behind.\
The vehicles continued to come, some representing several centuries of automotive optimism. Some were show-room polished while others appeared to need the sort of encouragement required by livestock and wayward relatives. One limousine coughed itself dead on the railway overpass and was pushed to the roundabout and onto the village mall.\
About an hour after the first Continental arrived, hourly trains from the city began disgorging Elvi in their hundreds, armed with guitar cases and suit bags, eskies and tents. The station checkpoint was overwhelmed with the arrival of each train. By the third train, a sit rep had reached Major Midler. Realising the futility of stopping the Elvi (unless he just shot them, which he wouldn\'92t because he was UDF not TRAMPS) he allowed the Elvi access right up to the Sublime Point gate, which had been closed at the exact time of the first trainload showing up. The Elvi were just more pieces on the major\'92s chess board, though he\'92d never played with guitar-carrying bishops and knights before. Nonetheless, he\'92d rather have the Elvi compressed south to Sublime Point than have them flanking him from the north.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 In the early afternoon, the
\f2\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2  
\f1\fs22 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 Elvi began electing camping sites so they could set their BBQs up and cook lunch. The golf club board were inundated with complaints of tents being pitched on the fairways and even some of the greens. One golfer rang to complain that a portable fridge on the fifteenth had denied her a hole-in-one.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Club security and the local private police force rushed out to keep the peace but were neutralised by the number of Elvi and by how charming they were. Clearly, solutions needed to be found. The Elvi set up improvised stages at approved places on the course grounds and promised to stage a show in the club house that night. They moved all their campsites to the rough where they were advised they would be safe from errant shots. After lunch, they assisted the ground staff with remedial repair of the damage they\'92d caused. As the Elvi spread the word of the Holy Momma, some residents blessed them as good, religious Latter Day Capitalists and offered spare wings of their mansions as accommodation through to Boxing Day. Others offered spare mansions. \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 After lunch, the Elvi discovered golf.\
A member\'92s son swapped his father\'92s golf clubs for a battered acoustic guitar, then traded the buggy and the bag for another guitar. More sets appeared, though most were loaned and few came under an exchange of contracts. Some of the golfer kids had been at the Rock Against Revival  and had become fervent Elvi fans, though their air guitars gathered dust unloved in closets and attics. Swinging their hips was second nature to the Elvi and soon many of them were taking practice swings and offering each other technical advice acquired during the previous eleven minutes. By mid afternoon they had tee times, which they respected with greater discipline than several military checkpoints were managing the traffic. Later, one promised Elvi performance in the clubhouse began late because the bass player was still on the back nine.\
Elvi players kept losing golf balls, which sometimes resulted in UDF troops emerging from the scrub rubbing their heads and elbows, and were even more confused when they were asked if they had come to praise the Dawkins. When the Elvi came to understand how many troops were hiding in the bush, they sent pulled pork and banana sandwiches in to feed them. Word went up the UDF command chain that the Elvi were trying to poison them, and the command came down to hold fire and burn the sandwiches.\
Some Airborne kids erected a sign behind the eighteenth green naming it the 
\fs20 HOLY MOMMA HOLE.
\fs22 \
Word got out that business was to be had. Coffee carts; ice-cream vans; trucks of camping supplies, blankets, batteries, rain capes, and portable chargers rolled through checkpoints unchallenged, as did food trucks selling fried products whose biological origins remained biological secrets. People who had packed enough food for themselves met people who had packed enough for twenty. Wherever Elvi remained stationary for more than half an hour, commerce formed around them.\
The 
\fs20 CAKE, BAGEL AND ROLL
\fs22  van arrived quietly stacked with nothing but band gear. \
Airborne kids from the city changed their holiday plans and came to visit friends and\'97tax forbid\'97family in the mountains. Old friendships morphed into the kind of opportunism usually associated with gold rushes and very large inheritances. One kid knew somebody whose parents had a house nearby. Somebody else had access to an empty deceased estate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Fathers watched through security cameras and took screenshots as their offspring opened side gates for kids who crossed their lawns carrying amplifiers. Private investigators could be hired later. Guitars appeared beside swimming pools in which Elvi waded, and towels were provided by staff. A guest wing of a neighbour\'92s was unlocked and thrown open; a mansion across the street was beset by enough musicians for three bands who argued about who had permission to move the keyboards.\
Colonel Tom Porker arrived and was floated over the clubhouse green in time to watch the sun go down. \
Hotels, motels, campgrounds, and Salvation Army halls filled for miles around. Spare rooms vanished into friendship networks of such complexity that hosts could identify neither the invited guests nor the Airborne teenager responsible for inviting them.\
As evening fell, the Elvi carried music into the village, bringing guitars, amplifiers, drums, and microphone stands. Punters crawled the pubs for the strongest bands and the most authentic Elvi cocktails. They played requests, signed things, then went to chill at parties in houses whose owners would spend the following week preparing insurance claims from security footage.\
}